{"seconds": 0.5263166250661016, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-repairs-v1/submissions/J08/gpt-5-2025-08-07/r1.json", "submission_sha256": "57355ca2812ef02fbdda62b6b5c2a142607d029a202e03f4b8bae73f21d9ce84", "code_sha256": "a0b92624fc09013cc7d2fe7c06e4fdf005d6b03ca2b187c17ef89a8927df4019", "description": "Learns a global intensity threshold and an object scale from annotated training patches, then performs seeded instance segmentation on each test image independently. Training uses only pixels within the valid ROI (channel1==1) and ignores unknown labels (train_y<0). The global threshold is chosen by maximizing pixel-wise F1 on a coarse grid across evenly subsampled training patches. Object scale is estimated as the median GT instance area; from this we derive a seed separation (local-max window) and a mild Gaussian smoothing sigma. For each test image: (1) smooth intensity; (2) threshold to a foreground mask inside geometric extent (channel1>0.5); (3) detect local maxima above a stricter peak level (peak_rel=max(thr+0.1, thr*1.15), clipped to 0.95) with non-maximum suppression window based on learned scale; (4) ensure at least one seed per connected foreground component by adding the brightest pixel if needed; (5) assign every foreground pixel to its nearest seed via an EDT-based Voronoi within the mask (watershed-equivalent over distance to seeds); (6) remove instances with area<4 pixels and relabel consecutively. Pixels outside the test extent mask are set to background 0. Each test image is processed separately; no attempt is made to reconcile labels across images or patches. Deterministic, single-thread friendly, uses only numpy/scipy.", "code_lines": 217, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

